<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turkish–Armenian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Turkish–Armenian War was fought from September to December 1920 between the Turkish nationalist forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey">Grand National Assembly</a> and the First Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. Turkish troops under Kâzım Karabekir took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> and Alexandropol, and Armenia was forced to sign the Treaty of Alexandropol, giving up Kars and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardahan">Ardahan</a>. Soon after, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> occupied Armenia, and the Treaty of Kars of 1921 confirmed the new border.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turkish-armenian-war.jpg" alt="Turkish–Armenian War" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User178198273998166172 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkish-Armenian_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
